(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Endodontic treatment carries risk of postoperative discomfort that may vary with) Tj
T*
(procedural technique. Accurate determination of working length--the distance from tooth) Tj
T*
(access to apical terminus--is fundamental to successful root canal completion. This study) Tj
T*
(will compare postoperative pain patterns following root canal treatment when working) Tj
T*
(length is established using one of several electronic detection systems versus traditional) Tj
T*
(radiographic methods. A total of 125 patients with asymptomatic irreversible pulpitis) Tj
T*
(affecting single-rooted teeth will be randomly allocated to five groups representing) Tj
T*
(different working length determination approaches: four distinct electronic locator brands) Tj
T*
(and conventional periapical radiography. A single operator will perform all treatments) Tj
T*
(using standardised instrumentation and filling techniques in single-visit appointments.) Tj
T*
(Pain intensity will be assessed via visual analogue rating at 6, 12, 24, and 48 hours) Tj
T*
(post-completion. Medication consumption will be documented. This design will clarify) Tj
T*
(whether working length detection methodology influences the magnitude or time-course of) Tj
T*
(postoperative pain.) Tj
